{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"05ac6f02ee6c982b1983bfd1294dec25cbde9e3b334ab76364f7c73207823821","packTokens":2305,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":843,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1103,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"failures","tokens":40,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"No test may count on those rows, because the app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Do not build screens here; the web app is built in its own repo.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authentication and authorization be enforced only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly requires them, or should additional access rules be added?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce only authentication/authorization requirements explicitly declared by contracts/openapi.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 13 requirements in one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 13 requirements be approved as one run, or should the work be split by cutting or deferring a part?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Apply only the lot-list filtering and security rules declared in contracts/openapi.yaml; add no authorizedYards restriction.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should lot-list responses apply an additional authorizedYards restriction beyond the filtering and security rules declared in the API contract?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Add separate cases for the contract-defined view-only and export-only paths, checking their respective redaction and export-denial behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the profitability permission checks be covered for users with view and export permissions independently?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate stock using opening stock and all persisted receipts, adjustments, and feeding events, incorporating the correction or void.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"After correcting or voiding a feeding event, how should the resulting stock be calculated when other persisted movements affect the same items?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"What must AC-10.2 verify after a confirmed sample reset or replacement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Verify the affected sample records were actually removed by reset or replaced by the replacement sample records, in addition to checking completion and recordCount.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"What should the sign-in acceptance criteria cover for incorrect credentials sent to POST /auth/sign-in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Add one case confirming incorrect credentials receive the contract-defined rejection response.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every path, HTTP method, parameter, request and response schema, status code, and security rule in the OpenAPI contract; expose no undocumented operations or product screens, and return 404 for undefined paths and 405 for unsupported methods.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined sign-in, session, dashboard, and filtered lot values, including declared permissions and authorized yards and correct ranking results; do not impose an extra authorized-yard restriction on matching lots, return contract-declared authentication errors, and do not deny authorized requests under undeclared role rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Return available procurement and receiving records, process imports with contract-defined matching results and allocation conflicts, and save allocations with PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, quantities, and capacity information; return the declared conflict or validation errors for invalid requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined lot forecasts, effective assumptions, metrics, and explainable insights, including null unavailable metric values; persist forecast-setting updates, planner actions, and weight measurements, return them in subsequent relevant responses, and use the declared validation or not-found errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Return contract-defined inventory totals, items, movements, stock fields, and projections for all supported horizons; persist valid inventory item and movement changes, return validation errors for invalid requests, and provide the requested CSV export as a Base64 file artifact.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Return saved ration definitions, persist valid ration creation and revision with calculated contract fields, provide optimization results and cost comparisons, and return approval results with the updated approval status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Return saved feed plans and their execution and audit fields; persist valid plan creation, review, and status changes with contract-defined calculated quantities, costs, energy, and status values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Persist feeding events and return their variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals; support corrections and voids with reconciled stock and totals that do not double-count event movements, and return the declared conflict or validation errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Return operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports using supported filters and contract-defined calculations, summaries, and exports; enforce the separate profitability view and export permissions, omit non-null profitability values when view access is absent, and return validation errors for missing required dates or unsupported export formats.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Return sample-data status and records, load samples without duplicates, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement; leave records unchanged when confirmation is absent and report the resulting status and records after confirmed operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the configured App PostgreSQL database, preserve successful writes across API restarts, and upgrade existing databases with required contract tables without changing existing row values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, run SeedData.Run at startup to add three to five believable, contract-example-derived rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing seed-write errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records only, return empty lists for empty collections, and allow tests to create and retrieve records without depending on demo-seed values or counts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-11 has an anchor that doesn't match the code\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}